\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces \begingroup \color  {claudecolor}MG detects component structure from scalar records. Left: regression with a known number of modes and fixed estimator settings across ranks. Center: learned generators with four output spectral lines but one (H4), two (M4), or four (T4) independent target phases; each dot is a seed. MG separates these tasks. Right: their full-state covariance participation ratios are similar. The comparison shows sensitivity to phase structure, which differs from the spread of variance measured by participation ratio.\endgroup }}{5}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:components}{{1}{5}{\claude {MG detects component structure from scalar records. Left: regression with a known number of modes and fixed estimator settings across ranks. Center: learned generators with four output spectral lines but one (H4), two (M4), or four (T4) independent target phases; each dot is a seed. MG separates these tasks. Right: their full-state covariance participation ratios are similar. The comparison shows sensitivity to phase structure, which differs from the spread of variance measured by participation ratio.}}{figure.1}{}}
